=== design notes (verified by probe) ===
  - `git merge --continue` DOES fire the commit-msg hook, and both
    FREELY_GUARDED_MERGE_COMPLETION=1 and the freely-guarded-merge-state file
    are visible to it. Hand merges have neither -> independent rejection point
    for a self-filled trailer. A direct probe confirmed this before wiring.
  - Real history: 25 recent commits checked against the general message rules
    (subject <=100 / no trailing period / blank second line / no trailing
    whitespace) -> 0 violations. Guarded develop merges all carry the full
    canonical trailer set, so wiring does not block normal work.
  - `commit-msg.sh` trailer extraction used `grep|tail` under `set -euo
    pipefail`: a MISSING trailer made the pipeline fail and aborted the hook
    BEFORE printing any rejection reason. Replaced with `sed -n ...p` (always
    succeeds) and routed every rejection heredoc to STDERR (git swallows hook
    stdout). Without this, CASE A was blocked silently with no reason.
  - Receipt-gated branches narrowed from `main|develop|test-pre-merge-*` to
    `main|develop`: every round syncs dev commits into the test-pre-merge
    sandbox with a plain merge, so requiring a guarded receipt there would
    self-lock wt-create/testing. Verified CASE D passes.
  - `.githooks/commit-msg` is byte-identical to the R8 fail-closed shim
    template (HOOK_NAME-driven), so it works with the 100644 truth script and
    exits 2 when the truth is missing. `.githooks/post-checkout` untouched.

=== boundary ===
  `governance-check` post-merge audit, pr-merge-guarded trailer writing and
  self-check were NOT modified; this PR only adds the missing submission-time
  layer so the self-check is no longer the only verification point.
  The `governance-check` merge_path allowlist mismatch (merge-guarded* vs
  pr-merge-guarded*) was reviewed as a separate defect candidate and is NOT
  bundled; no new raw issue was filed because it needs a separate scope review.
